'' 'offsetof( T, field )' BESIDE A PROCEDURE OF THE FIELD'S NAME. layout's interface replays
'' hdr/rec.ti, so the header's '#assert offsetof( Rec, span_ )' is compiled inside edits too,
'' where edits' private 'Span_' is in scope; Resolve walked the field as an expression, bound
'' the procedure, and it was TKO0776 "argument 1 of 'span_' is left out" (tkEdit's private
'' 'Len_' against posix's 'struct_inotify_event.len_', Linux). main's own 'Span_', declared
'' before its 'offsetof', is the one-file shape. fbc-modern 1.20 prints 4 for the offset.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: -target windows-x86_64 -i toolchains/tiko-windows/inc tests/modules/src/offsetprivproc/main.tiko -o tests/modules/offsetprivproc.exe
'' ENV: TIKO_LIBPATH=build/obj/rtlib/windows-x86_64
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-NOT: TKO0776
'' RUN: tests/modules/offsetprivproc.exe
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT:  42 5 4 103
